commit_sha":"a45d4fec5d463563b3273e4d682a79b427db3369","position":"1786248467529374001-11a41b09-9e70-4ec1-97e5-8fc7e13f8547"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f6c34a9e7c29c493a6c8aae4b77a0fb7d5ffef8800467752d58f57018e015803","event_uuid":"06dabb8b-9b47-4276-ac99-4fe7b0b90bcb","position":{"commit_sha":"150220ccc5b64da46706870948c61c55912eadb2","position":"1786248479595423001-06dabb8b-9b47-4276-ac99-4fe7b0b90bcb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"256811581b11471f6d0f4ff059d12a4ea118a4d3b3b689730a8514fb6098f496","event_uuid":"5903dce7-7edf-466e-8ce9-cdf42a7335d8","position":{"commit_sha":"b2104709d4af80a3392eb47762ae7fd5db86abb7","position":"1786248686034263001-5903dce7-7edf-466e-8ce9-cdf42a7335d8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"81f3b2a205399400596ba72fa9cc18c93ad410cedb2c8348124031f7b9ac2c53","event_uuid":"003961f0-09e7-46fe-af87-74fc4f762e48","position":{"commit_sha":"820129fd3cbcd53ca1ac0ae097f9910979a61eb0","position":"1786248920898882001-003961f0-09e7-46fe-af87-74fc4f762e48"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"21653ffc3692ef16fe2adffbea340c37f9c6ae471ccac8996861929cad70bba1","event_uuid":"9e08e0bc-c131-4513-9581-311887b6f985","position":{"commit_sha":"d34467622780ea5e6ec4362d7a16f7ff1029a664","position":"1786250612071913001-9e08e0bc-c131-4513-9581-311887b6f985"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PHASE 1 COMPLETE — proven root cause and caller-safety gate\n\nRoot cause: Python 3.11 asyncio.wait_for has the documented cancellation/completion race in CPython issue 86296. In src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py:76-85 the worker awaits wait_for(asyncio.to_thread(...)); TestClient shutdown cancels that worker at app.py:55-59. When the offloaded fake completes in the same turn, Python 3.11 tasks.py:477-479 returns the child result instead of re-raising the external CancelledError. The worker therefore updates the record, executes queue.task_done(), and loops back to the empty queue with cancelling()==1. Lifespan issued only one cancel and awaits that still-live task without a bound, so Starlette never receives lifespan.shutdown.complete and pytest-timeout kills the worker. Python 3.12 rewrote wait_for on asyncio.timeout and does not consume this cancellation.\n\nRuntime proof:\n- Deterministic no-thread/no-TestClient harness, identical real _worker: Python 3.11 after release+cancel => done=False, cancelled=False, cancelling=1, record_status=completed, stack=_worker at the next queue read. Python 3.12 => done=True, cancelled=True, record_status=running. This rules out xdist, TestClient, AnyIO, executor shutdown, and shared app state.\n- Tagged real-path trace on the original test under Python 3.11 observed lifespan cancel (task pending), then wait_for returned with current_task().cancelling()==1, then the worker looped; lifespan never joined and the 3s watchdog fired. Python 3.12 joined promptly. All instrumentation was removed; worktree is clean.\n- Intervention probe replaced only Python 3.11 wait_for with Python 3.12 asyncio.timeout semantics: the original target passed 20/20; unpatched baseline failed 3/3.\n- Executor alternative rejected for this incident: a deliberately blocked run_job propagated worker CancelledError and joined lifespan before portal teardown; its executor thread was visibly blocked. The actual failure had an idle executor thread and was still waiting for lifespan shutdown.\n\nThe account explains the CI timing: three Ubuntu/Python 3.11 runs reached the 300s per-test timeout then reported node down on test_matching_guard_is_accepted, while Python 3.12/3.13 passed. The local target reproduces without xdist; xdist only reports the killed worker.\n\nDefect legitimacy: app.py:1-7 promises ACK-fast bounded job processing, app.py:62-66 says no job can wedge the queue, and the existing matching-guard TestClient contract at tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py:44-50,137-144 must teardown. This is a defect, not intended behavior.\n\nCaller/dependency sweep: _worker has one caller, opcert lifespan. The app is hosted by uvicorn through infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert and exercised by test_opcert_service_app.py; no caller behaviorally depends on a consumed cancellation or unbounded shutdown. Expected post-fix behavior: a shutdown cancellation always terminates the worker promptly even when job completion collides with it; accepted-job semantics, per-job timeout behavior, status schemas, and Python 3.12+ behavior remain unchanged.","timestamp":1786248407658467001}],"created_at":1786231574046402001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"799a0571-c96e-4bbc-a093-fe44b4c63131","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b014-1526-16d0-4c3f"},{"link_uuid":"ddbf8947-5e63-4c26-9cab-7cfbe99e93cc","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"424f-bc35-b7ca-419a"},{"link_uuid":"9e08e0bc-c131-4513-9581-311887b6f985","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"93ba-9e5c-f741-40d7"},{"link_uuid":"4defac72-fa22-4c41-b60b-be8989cd01fe","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0653-f8c0-b370-4a13"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nPython 3.11 CI intermittently kills an xdist worker after `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py::test_matching_guard_is_accepted` hangs in TestClient teardown. Three recent runs hit the 300-second hang guard; Python 3.12/3.13 pass. The exact mechanism and runtime proof are recorded in the Phase 1 RCA comment.\n\n## Proven mechanism\n\nPython 3.11 `asyncio.wait_for` can consume an external worker cancellation when its child future completes in the same turn (CPython issue 86296). The opcert worker then loops back to `queue.get()` with a pending cancellation count, while lifespan awaits it forever. A deterministic harness observed that state; replacing only `wait_for` with Python 3.12-style timeout semantics made the original reproduction pass 20/20.\n\n## Phase 2 plan\n\n- Inventory the existing opcert app coverage and freeze a contract card for prompt lifespan teardown when a job completion collides with shutdown cancellation.\n- Add the smallest Python-3.11 regression oracle in `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py`; prove it RED for the cancellation-completion mechanism before production changes.\n- Hold that oracle out from the fixer. Repair the cancellation mechanism in `src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py` while preserving the 202 ACK, terminal record schema, one-worker queue, per-job timeout, and Python 3.12+ behavior.\n- Restore the held-out oracle; prove GREEN, seed the exact swallowed-cancellation defect and prove RED again, then restore the fix.\n- Run the opcert app/core suites under Python 3.11 and the pinned Python 3.12 environment, plus lint, typecheck, complexity/module-size, and the broader relevant suite.\n- Replicate the original lone-test and xdist scenarios; sweep other `asyncio.wait_for(asyncio.to_thread(...))` lifecycle sites and parallel app surfaces for the confirmed pattern.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A regression oracle is observed RED before the fix and GREEN after it on Python 3.11.\n- [ ] Shutdown cancellation terminates the opcert worker promptly even when job completion collides with cancellation.\n- [ ] The held-out oracle returns RED under an exact defect-seeded mutation, then GREEN after restoration.\n- [ ] The original lone-test and xdist reproductions no longer hang on Python 3.11.\n- [ ] Existing opcert semantics and Python 3.12+ tests remain green; lint and typecheck pass.\n- [ ] RCA, proof, caller safety, sibling sweep, and final verification are recorded on this ticket.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py","reason":"repair Python 3.11 worker cancellation-completion race during lifespan shutdown"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py","reason":"held-out RED-to-GREEN regression oracle for prompt teardown at the proven race"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0653-f8c0-b370-4a13"],["relates_to","93ba-9e5c-f741-40d7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b6aa6171-0f02-4054-b6b9-1fa68c11721c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2207-2917-e21b-42bd","ticket_type":"bug","title":"py3.11 xdist worker crash: opcert test_matching_guard_is_accepted","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["115cc739-4f5e-448a-a09f-9898d10a27bd","799a0571-c96e-4bbc-a093-fe44b4c63131","ddbf8947-5e63-4c26-9cab-7cfbe99e93cc","ed4ed86f-3ac1-445c-b5de-46c0ffeca941","b6aa6171-0f02-4054-b6b9-1fa68c11721c","4ebb2e82-b2e4-46c3-be16-09ee8ca8c8dd","a26c4a26-49a5-4a55-828b-05ca040e046a","11a41b09-9e70-4ec1-97e5-8fc7e13f8547","06dabb8b-9b47-4276-ac99-4fe7b0b90bcb","5903dce7-7edf-466e-8ce9-cdf42a7335d8","003961f0-09e7-46fe-af87-74fc4f762e48","9e08e0bc-c131-4513-9581-311887b6f985","4defac72-fa22-4c41-b60b-be8989cd01fe"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786250842632097714,"uuid":"9545f4cd-6258-446f-9142-7b2dc108fbac"}